I walk further into the market and stop at a clothing stall.
I see a heavy winter coat made of wool.
This coat is beautiful, but very thick.
I try the coat on anyway.
It is incredibly warm.
I take it off again immediately.
It is July, and the sun is shining today.
A friendly woman stands behind the table and smiles.
"Is it too warm?" the woman asks.
"Yes, it is a bit too warm for the summer," I reply and laugh.
I touch the thick fabric.
"But I really needed this winter coat five months ago!" I say.
The woman laughs loudly.
"Yes, February was very cold," she says.
I remember my first weeks in Copenhagen.
I was constantly freezing back then.
Fortunately, I do not need such warm clothes right now.
I hang the coat back on the rack and say goodbye.
